  "notes": "24K Derate (TO-1) takeoff V-speeds, both dry and wet runway, transcribed from FCOM PI.30.15 (dry, p.1071) and PI.30.16 (wet, p.1072), 737-800/CFM56-7B26. STRUCTURAL DIFFERENCE from the 26K (full-rated) source files: the 26K data was split into two sibling files (takeoff_vspeeds_dry.json / takeoff_vspeeds_wet.json), each with the full top-level shape (source/unit/max_takeoff_thrust_v1_vr_v2/temp_press_alt_adjustment/slope_wind_v1_adjustment/v1_mcg) directly at the file root. This file instead nests that identical per-condition shape under top-level 'dry' and 'wet' keys in a single file, per the task's file list (only one takeoff_vspeeds_to1.json was requested, covering both runway conditions). Each of out['dry'] and out['wet'] is otherwise shaped exactly like the existing dry/wet 26K files' root. Also note the slope_wind_v1_adjustment weight axis here is only 6 points (84,76,68,60,52,44) vs the 26K file's 6 points (90,80,70,60,50,40) -- both tables use a coarser weight axis than the main V1/VR/V2 table's 11-point axis, consistent with the source FCOM page layout. V1(MCG) is identical between dry and wet (same behavior as the 26K/full-rated tables)."
